      "message": "Can you help me come up with a better name for this? As it stands `dp_is_active(port) \u003d\u003d false` does not imply that `dp_is_inactive(port) \u003d\u003d true`, and I don\u0027t really want to put that in the codebase. Maybe it makes sense to change the name of `dp_is_active.`\n\nThe actual concepts are something like\n* `dp_is_active`: DP entry is done, and the port is in DP alt mode. DP exit may be about to start but hasn\u0027t really started yet.\n* `dp_is_inactive` (new): DP entry has not started, or DP exit has already finished.\n* `dp_entry_is_done`: DP entry has completed successfully, or DP exit has completed, successfully or otherwise.",
